{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "המלאה", :translit "ha-m'le'ah", :gloss "the fill"} {:he "פן תקדש המלאה", :translit "pen tikdash ha-m'le'ah", :gloss "lest it be sanctified, the fill"} {:he "כאשר תעיק העגלה המלאה", :translit "ka'asher ta'ik ha'agalah ha-m'le'ah", :gloss "as the cart presses down, the fill"} {:he "לה עמיר", :translit "lah amir", :gloss "to it, sheaves"} {:he "בכלאים", :translit "b'kil'ayim", :gloss "in kilayim"} {:he "כמלא צמד בקר", :translit "k'mlo tza'med bakar", :gloss "like the fill of a yoke of cattle"} {:he "בד\"א שוחקות", :translit "bd\"a shokakot", :gloss "by relaxation of the legs"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["פן תקדש המלאה" "כאשר תעיק העגלה המלאה"]}], :frame {:text "The halakhic measure for distance required between diverse seeds (kil'ayim) is defined as the area needed to work a yoke of cattle, which the Talmud terms כמלא צמד בקר (Kilayim 2:9, Shabbat 85a). The Ba'al HaTurim reads the doubled occurrence of המלאה as a masoretic signpost pointing to that measure: one instance refers to כמלא צמד בקר and the other to לה עמיר. The phrase בד\"א שוחקות refers to the Talmudic discussion of how this space is measured when the team of animals is not pulling taut (Shabbat 85a). The phonological note about the dagesh concerns whether the letter bet in the word המלאה carries a dagesh, which would signal that the word is pronounced with a hard bet rather than a soft one.", :sources ["Kilayim 2:9" "Shabbat 85a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["פן תקדש המלאה" "כאשר תעיק העגלה המלאה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "פן תקדש המלאה", :refs ["Deuteronomy 22:9"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כאשר תעיק העגלה המלאה", :refs ["Amos 2:13"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:38:20.024802574Z", :model "glm-5.2"}